# ============================================================================
# RELEASE SCAFFOLDING — INTENTIONALLY DISABLED (.disabled suffix + commented)
#
# This workflow is inert until your app is ready to ship to Jamf Self Service
# via the psd-sign pipeline (sign → notarize → staple → pkgbuild → notarize
# pkg → verify). It is modeled on PSD401/atrium-capture's release-macos.yml,
# the flagship pattern for district macOS releases.
#
# The `.disabled` suffix keeps GitHub Actions from parsing the file: a
# comments-only .yml in .github/workflows/ registers a FAILING "workflow file
# issue" run on every push (verified: run 31853130309 on this repo).
#
# To activate:
#   1. Write a `scripts/build-macos-pkg.sh` that wraps the SPM binary in a
#      .app bundle (Info.plist, icon), signs it with the Developer ID
#      Application identity, notarizes, staples, builds the .pkg with the
#      Developer ID Installer identity, and notarizes the pkg — or run the
#      psd-sign skill locally to generate one. atrium-capture's script is the
#      reference implementation.
#   2. Confirm the org MACOS_* secrets are available to this repo:
#        MACOS_DEVELOPER_ID_APPLICATION_P12 / _PASSWORD
#        MACOS_DEVELOPER_ID_INSTALLER_P12 / _PASSWORD
#        MACOS_BUILD_KEYCHAIN_PASSWORD
#        MACOS_NOTARY_PRIVATE_KEY / MACOS_NOTARY_KEY_ID / MACOS_NOTARY_ISSUER_ID
#   3. Rename this file to release-macos.yml, uncomment everything below
#      this header block, and adjust names/paths.
#   4. Hand the notarized .pkg to Technology Services for Jamf Self Service.
# ============================================================================
#
